    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d31">

                <pb facs="0086" n="56" xml:id="pg56"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Lot 71–D 440, Box 19230</note>
                <anchor n="1" xml:id="d31-f1"/>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by Mr. Carl M. Marcy of the United States
                        Delegation Staff of Advisers to the Principal Executive Officer of the
                        Delegation</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sandifer</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">New
                                York</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian" when="1947-09-12"
                            >September 12, 1947</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Subject: Headquarters Agreement and Privileges and
                    Immunities</p>
                <p>Mr. Fahy and I discussed this morning the advisability of having our political
                    officers informed as soon as possible that we want the Headquarters Agreement
                    approved by the General Assembly without change. As you know, the Agreement has
                    been approved by the Congress and it would be most unfortunate if it were
                    necessary for us to go back to Congress next year with a different agreement.
                    Political officers should be informed that the privileges and immunities granted
                    to the United Nations in the Headquarters Agreement are most certainly broader
                    than those which would be acceptable to our Congress next year.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
